{%- doc -%}
  SoulStruck — the URL a product card should link to.

  The theme linked cards with `variant.url`, which is `/products/handle?variant=<id>`
  for Shopify's auto-selected first variant. Landing on the product page with a
  variant already in the URL defeats the "Choose Your Kit" gate: `product.selected_variant`
  is set, so the price shows, Add to cart is live, and the shopper is never asked to
  pick a kit they never picked.

  For a multi-variant product this outputs the clean `/products/handle` instead, so the
  product page opens in its unselected state. Single-variant products keep the theme's
  original variant URL, since there is nothing to choose.

  A kit the shopper DID pick on the card is still carried through — assets/ss-variant-cards.js
  rewrites any [data-ss-product-link] href to ?variant=<chosen id> on selection.

  @param {object} product - The product object
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ss_multi = false
  unless product.has_only_default_variant
    if product.variants.size > 1
      assign ss_multi = true
    endif
  endunless

  if ss_multi
    echo product.url
  else
    echo product.selected_or_first_available_variant.url
  endif
-%}
